window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"cassiopeia","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your grounding W comes online — Miasma kills Ashen Pursuit, the only mobility he owns, in both directions."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Base ults trade evenly at 120 seconds each: your Gaze answers his commit if you are facing the right way."},{"when":"1st item","text":"The danger stage — Ashen Pursuit flanks around your Gaze into Purgatory's execute. Ward the side brushes."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your ramping DPS finally matches his burst profile — the lane math evens back out."}],"wants":{"you":["Poison-stacked E grinding","W on his approach path","Flank wards before fights"],"foe":["Punish your W cooldown","Flank angles past your Gaze","Chip you to execute range"]},"early":"An even but twitchy lane. His on-hit walk-ups sting your thin frame, so make him pay for every approach: Q on his path, then E him while poison ticks. Your E needs that poison setup, so don't spam it raw. From 3 on, drop W where he has to cross — grounding kills the 10-second Ashen Pursuit.","mid":"Level 6 opens an even ult war — your Gaze answers his commit if you are facing him. His first item is the danger stage: Ashen Pursuit flanks around your Gaze into Purgatory, so ward the side brushes, keep your back to walls, and hold W to ground the angle. Never sit at execute-range HP.","late":"Two-plus items your ramping DPS finally matches his burst profile and the lane math evens. In fights, you win everywhere he can't reach you in one jump: W the flank, save Gaze for the moment he shows, and melt him with stacked E's if he ever commits front-on. Sidelane only with flanks warded.","whys":["Level 1 is even — his on-hit trades sting your squishy frame, but your Q poke makes his walk-up expensive; nobody trades for free.","Level 2 stays even: your E needs poison up before it pays, so trades stay short and honest on both sides.","Level 3 is a wash that revolves around Miasma — ground Ashen Pursuit on his approach and you win the exchange, miss and he closes for free.","Levels 4-5 stay even — he hunts your W cooldown windows while you punish every approach with Q-into-E poison grinding.","Level 6 opens even: base ults and totems roughly trade, and your Gaze keeps his straightforward engages honest.","First item is Locke's — a flanking E around your Gaze into Purgatory beats you. Ward the flanks, hug walls and never fight at execute-range health.","Late settles even as your ramping DPS meets his burst: he kills you through one clean pick, you melt him through one landed Gaze."]});
