window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"cassiopeia","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"His spike — Aureate Rush (E, 10s) closes the gap before your slow ever stacks and your escapeless kit cannot disengage."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Petrifying Gaze evens it: face his Aureate Rush and the all-in ends in a stun and a corpse."},{"when":"1st item","text":"He forces 1v1s your escapeless kit loses and Dreaded Return yanks you in — shove from range."},{"when":"Late","text":"He wins the duel, and Grim Deliverance heals him — carry anti-heal, group, and melt him through chokes."}],"wants":{"you":["Q slow before he leaps","Gaze facing his engage","Teamfights over duels"],"foe":["E onto you at 2-3","Straight 1v1s at items","Side angles around Gaze"]},"early":"Open even and farming — you poke, he stays out of Twin Fang range. The cliff is level 2: Aureate Rush (E) closes the gap on a 10s cooldown before your slow stacks, and you have no escape. Play behind the wave and hoard Miasma for that dash, not for poke — grounded, his only way in dies. Level 3 is worse; hug tower until 4-5.","mid":"Petrifying Gaze changes the conversation at 6 — face him when he commits and his all-in ends in a stun and a corpse, so hold it for the engage. Respect Dreaded Return (W, 14s): the pull drags an escapeless Cassiopeia into melee, so never line up with him. He forces 1v1s at first item your kit loses; refuse them and shove from range.","late":"He out-duels you at two-plus items and there is no pretending otherwise — but you outscale him in every fight that matters. Carry Grievous Wounds: Glaive and Grim Deliverance both heal him. Group, W the chokepoints, and melt his frontline with ramped fangs from behind your team.","whys":["Level 1 is even — you poke from distance and he farms outside Twin Fang range, with neither able to force more.","Zaahen spikes at 2: Aureate Rush (E) closes the gap on a 10s cooldown before your slow stacks, and your escapeless kit cannot disengage.","Level 3 is his — an immobile Cassiopeia has no answer to a walk-up with Aureate Rush and Dreaded Return both up. Hug your tower.","Levels 4-5 even out: your Q slow and ramped E damage finally make bad approaches expensive, so his engages stop being free.","At 6 it's even — Petrifying Gaze stuns his advance if he comes in face-on, which forces his all-in to get creative or stay home.","First item is Zaahen's: he forces straight 1v1s your kit cannot escape, and Glaive plus Grim Deliverance heal him through your poison grind.","Two-plus items he still wins the duel — you've become a teamfight monster, but the sidelane stays his, so never test it alone."]});
